@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2060 = private unnamed_addr constant [578 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for indentation that uses tabs.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAccording to [PEP 8], spaces are preferred over tabs (unless used to remain\0Aconsistent with code that is already indented with tabs).\0A\0A## Formatter compatibility\0AWe recommend against using this rule alongside the [formatter]. The\0Aformatter enforces consistent indentation, making the rule redundant.\0A\0AThe rule is also incompatible with the [formatter] when using\0A`format.indent-style=\22tab\22`.\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#tabs-or-spaces\0A[formatter]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter\0A", align 1
