@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2102 = private unnamed_addr constant [584 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for bidirectional unicode characters.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe interaction between bidirectional unicode characters and the\0Asurrounding code can be surprising to those that are unfamiliar\0Awith right-to-left writing systems.\0A\0AIn some cases, bidirectional unicode characters can also be used to\0Aobfuscate code and introduce or mask security vulnerabilities.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0As = \22\D7\90\22 * 100  #  \22\D7\90\22 is assigned\0Aprint(s)  # prints a 100-character string\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 672: Bidirectional Text](https://peps.python.org/pep-0672/#bidirectional-text)\0A", align 1
